          "p": "One honest thing first, because it shapes this whole chapter. Søren Kierkegaard wrote in Danish, and every English translation of his major works is still in copyright, which means he is the one major thinker in this whole long story we cannot quote directly. So everything in this chapter is in our own words, his ideas restated rather than his sentences reproduced, with the key terms given in his own Danish where they carry weight. That is a real loss, and worth naming once, because Kierkegaard of all people wrote in sentences built to ambush you. Take the restatements as faithful, not verbatim."
